      "message": "We\u0027ve had a problem with the idletimer target ever since some code was merged upstream around ~5.6 and later 5.10/mainline picked it up via upstream merge with incorrect conflict resolution.\n\nI\u0027m of the opinion that we should entirely revert back to upstream for 5.10+, then reapply a clean patch and make sure it makes sense this time around.  I\u0027ve been meaning to do this... but... I don\u0027t actually understand what the IDLETIMER target does, nor what the true requirements are, and we have no unit tests.\n\nAs such I think a core requirement is going to be to write some sort of kernel net/tests unit test before we merge anything.",
